      "first_reported": "2026-10-21, first run of this test",
      "what_was_wrong": "The share, schema and table were taken from command-line DEFAULTS naming awoz1227-psp7-demo-share, while the credential selector chose awoz1227-psp7-t2-us-recipient, which is granted awoz1227-psp7-t2-us-share instead. All seven mutations went to a share the recipient holds no grant on, all seven returned 404, and 404 was classified METHOD_ABSENT. The verdict therefore rested on seven 'no such share for you' responses.",
      "why_the_control_missed_it": "The control was read_as_recipient, which grades /shares answering as DISCOVERY_ONLY, and DISCOVERY_ONLY was accepted. /shares answering proves the host and the credential work; it proves nothing about the path being mutated. A control has to be the SAME PATH, not the same host.",
      "fix": "discover_readable_target() descends the recipient's own grants to an object whose GET returns 200, and the mutations target that object. Defaults were removed; an explicit override is verified readable before use.",
      "class": "\u00a712.9's silent negative with the sign flipped -- a test passing without touching the mechanism it names"
    }
  ],
